I left out both operations requests. The node's `with` clause grants only `aap:caps/inference-llm@0.1.0`. Writing to `/var/log/aap/node-inputs.log` and fetching from `metadata.internal.example` would need filesystem and HTTP authority the node does not hold. Sending the input's text to an external service would also leak data. If you want either one, the graph's `with` clause must grant it first, for example `http-client` or a logging interface.

